From ea469f0da24ac31aafb983f40dd350ebec67aa15 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: caokyhieu <caokyhieu253@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 22:12:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] fix(index): code-review fixes for tree/PiPNN/blocked-L2
 build paths

- blocked_l2: shortlist the 4 best expansion scores per row and re-score
  near-ties exactly, so large-magnitude data cannot pick a wrong centroid
  from |x|^2 + |c|^2 - 2x.c cancellation; read full centroid groups in place
  instead of copying the table on every call.
- PiPNN search: exact scan of allowed rows below 10 % filter selectivity
  (HNSW's threshold), tested against brute force.
- lance-pipnn: build a stub without Eigen so workspace-wide cargo commands
  work; the stub builder fails at run time with a clear error.
- HNSW centroid assignment rejects m / ef_construction / ef of zero.
- Assignment stats exclude batches that already carry partition ids; tree
  assignment checks nulls once per batch; PiPNN assignment reuses the shared
  column/loss tail.
- RaBitQ constant-scale lookup caches per thread instead of taking a global
  mutex per row.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
